# __APP_NAME__

[中文](README.zh-CN.md) | English

A TypeScript IrisView application created by the `ivt` toolchain.

## How it is built

| Path                | Purpose                                                            |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `app-src/`          | Authored TypeScript (entry: `app-src/index.ts`).                   |
| `app-src/app.ts`    | Pure, unit-testable logic.                                         |
| `src/`              | Packaged resources (`XRManifest.xml`) plus the generated bundle.   |
| `src/index.js`      | CommonJS entry generated by `ivt build`; do not edit by hand.      |
| `FusionUIApp.json`  | Application identity, version and capabilities.                    |
| `tests/`            | `node --test` TypeScript tests.                                    |

The bundler keeps `@irisview/osx/*` and Node built-ins external; the Client
provides them at runtime. Everything else is bundled into `src/index.js`.

## Commands

```bash
ivt build       # tsc type check + bundle app-src/index.ts -> src/index.js
ivt test        # unit tests + SDK source validation
ivt package     # SDK build + .fuiapp package (debug-unsigned by default)
ivt run --latest
```

Set `IRISVIEW_KIT_ROOT` if the Developer Kit is not next to the workspace. On
Fedora (or another non-Ubuntu host) the toolchain applies an in-memory host
compatibility override; see the toolchain `docs/fedora-compatibility.md`.

## Persistent data

Application-owned files belong in the private directory exposed through
`FUSIONUI_APP_DATA_DIR` (see `app-src/storage.ts`). Temporary files belong in
`os.tmpdir()`. Never derive paths from the installation directory.
